##DESCRIPTION
##  Middle School problem:
##ENDDESCRIPTION

## ProblemTester('Laura Travis')
## Publisher('Prentice Hall')
## DBsubject(Arithmetic)
## DBchapter(Fractions/rational numbers)
## DBsection(Addition/subtraction)
## Date(11/12/2012)
## Institution(Mississippi College)
## Author(John Travis)
## MLT(subtract_fracs_diff_denom)
## MLTleader(1)
## Level(2)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('Pre-Algebra')
## KEYWORDS('prealgebra','common core','fractions')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'contextFraction.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Fraction-NoDecimals");
Context()->flags->set(reduceFractions => 0);

$atop = random(19, 25);
$abot = random(6,  9);
$btop = random(11, 18);
$bbot = $abot + random(-1, 1, 2);

$ans = Compute("($atop*$bbot-$btop*$abot)/($abot*$bbot)");

Context()->operators->undefine("-", "+");

BEGIN_PGML

Add the following and express your answer as a single fraction.  No decimals or mixed fractions.

>>
[`` \frac{[$atop]}{[$abot]} - \frac{[$btop]}{[$bbot]} = ``] [_]{$ans}
<<

END_PGML

$showHint = 3;
BEGIN_PGML_HINT
First you will need to get a common denominator by finding the least common multiple.

END_PGML_HINT

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
First, a common denominator must be found.  Since there are no common factors between the denominators, the product is the common denominator
[``` 
\begin{aligned}
\frac{[$atop]}{[$abot]} - \frac{[$btop]}{[$bbot]} & = 
\frac{[$atop]}{[$abot]}\cdot \frac{[$bbot]}{[$bbot]} - 
\frac{[$btop]}{[$bbot]}\cdot \frac{[$abot]}{[$abot]} \\
& = \frac{[$atop*$bbot]}{[$abot*$bbot]} - 
\frac{[$btop*$abot]}{[$abot*$bbot]}  \\
& = [$ans]
\end{aligned}
```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();        